  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ashish Kumar Agarwal & Anr vs State Of Rajasthan & Anr on 20 April, 2015 Author: Vijay Bishnoi",
    "facts": "This criminal misc. petition under Section 482 Cr.P.C. has been filed by the petitioners being aggrieved with the order dated 14.03.2015 whereby the Additional District Magistrate-cum- Adjudicating Officer, Sirohi has imposed a fine of Rs.2,00,000/- upon the petitioner-firm in the proceedings under clause (ii) of Sub-Section (2) of Section 26 and Sections 51 and 52 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Learned counsel for the petitioners has submitted that expiry date of seized food items was April 2013 whereas for the first time, the petitioner was given notice by the authorized officer in December 2013. It is contended that right of the petitioners, to ask for sending the remaining part of the seized articles to be analyzed by accredited food laboratory, has been infringed because such opportunity was given to the petitioners after the expiry date of seized articles.",
